From: OnePlus 7 Pro bring-up <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: msm-poweroff: add qcom,poweroff-only and run first

On the OnePlus 7 Pro, power off through PSCI SYSTEM_OFF ends in a PMIC hard
reset: the bootloader reports androidboot.startupmode=hard_reset and the
phone starts again. The PMIC power key driver already sets the PS_HOLD reset
type to shutdown before power off, so pulling PS_HOLD low directly (what the
downstream kernel does) switches the phone off.

Add a "qcom,poweroff-only" property so a board can use PS_HOLD for power off
without taking over restart from PSCI, and run the PS_HOLD power off handler
before the legacy PSCI pm_power_off hook.
---
--- a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
@@ -29,11 +29,19 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(msm_ps_hold))
 		return PTR_ERR(msm_ps_hold);
 
-	devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
-				      128, do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
+	/*
+	 * On some boards (OnePlus 7 Pro) PSCI SYSTEM_OFF ends in a PMIC hard
+	 * reset instead of a shutdown, while pulling PS_HOLD low directly
+	 * shuts the PMIC down as the PS_HOLD reset type was set by the
+	 * PMIC power key driver. Such boards keep PSCI for restart and only
+	 * use PS_HOLD for power off.
+	 */
+	if (!of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,poweroff-only"))
+		devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
+					      128, do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
 
 	devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_POWER_OFF,
-				      SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT, do_msm_poweroff,
+				      SYS_OFF_PRIO_HIGH, do_msm_poweroff,
 				      NULL);
 
 	return 0;
